From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Foundation Classes - size math_Uzawa's initial-error vector by
 the constraint count

math_Uzawa stores the initial error Cont*StartingPoint - Secont, which has one
entry per constraint, in a vector sized by the number of unknowns:

  Errinit(1, Cont.ColNumber()),

Both constructors do it, and Perform then writes the whole thing by row:

  for (i = 1; i <= Nlig; i++)        // Nlig = Cont.RowNumber()
    Errinit(i) = Cont(i, 1) * StartingPoint(1) - Secont(i);

Every other use of Errinit is a row index too: the Cont*T(Cont) solve at the
direct branch reads Errinit(j) for j up to Nlig, and the iterative branch reads
Errinit(i) over the same range. The accessor is declared as "the initial error
Cont*StartingPoint-Secont", so RowNumber() is the length the class documents.

An overdetermined system, more constraints than unknowns, therefore writes past
the end of Errinit. math_Vector inlines 32 doubles, so the outcome depends on
size rather than on validity: 4 constraints and 2 unknowns reports IsDone and a
wrong answer, 33 and 32 writes one slot past the inlined buffer, 40 and 33 runs
seven past a heap block, and 100 and 2 is a deterministic SIGSEGV. The
dimension check at the top of Perform does not catch any of them, because it
relates Secont and Nce + Nci to the row count and never relates rows to
columns.

The three sibling members are already sized correctly and are left alone: Resul
and Erruza are indexed by unknown, Vardua and CTCinv by constraint.

math_Uzawa.cxx defines No_Standard_OutOfRange and No_Standard_DimensionError
itself, at the top of the file, so NCollection_Array1's own inline bounds check
is compiled out here even in a debug build and nothing reports the overrun.

Reported as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#2860.

diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/math/math_Uzawa.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/math/math_Uzawa.cxx
index 0bbf9589..f903d737 100644
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/math/math_Uzawa.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/math/math_Uzawa.cxx
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
                        const int          NbIterations)
     : Resul(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
       Erruza(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
-      Errinit(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
+      Errinit(1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       Vardua(1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       CTCinv(1, Cont.RowNumber(), 1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       NbIter(0),
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
                        const int          NbIterations)
     : Resul(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
       Erruza(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
-      Errinit(1, Cont.ColNumber()),
+      Errinit(1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       Vardua(1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       CTCinv(1, Cont.RowNumber(), 1, Cont.RowNumber()),
       NbIter(0),
